e 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere with crew. Strengths: reliability, decision speed, crew atmosphere. Concerns: communication, egocentric, lack of development.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership, weak leadership, arrogance.\n\nWe need best overall fit. Likely candidate B has strong technical and stress, but cooperation concerns. Candidate C has reliability and crew atmosphere but communication issues. Candidate A has anticipation and leadership but organization issues. Candidate D has problem solving and responsibility but arrogance and weak leadership.\n\nWhich is best? Long-distance pilot requires reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, decision quality, crew cooperation, communication, responsibility. Candidate B: strong on stress, conscientious (reliability), technical (computer, weather), but uncooperative and grumpy - crew cooperation may suffer. Candidate C: reliability, decision speed, positive crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric may affect crew cooperation. Candidate A: anticipation, complex connections, leadership, but unorganized and poor at criticism - could affect reliability and teamwork. Candidate D: problem solving, concentration, responsibility, but arrogance and weak leadership - may affect crew.\n\nProbably candidate B is strongest overall despite cooperation concerns; but we need to discuss. As first contribution, we can propose candidate B, citing strengths and acknowledging concerns, and suggest need to verify cooperation. Provide recommendation.\n\nWe must include METADATA_JSON with vote.\n\nProceed."}
